---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Stream a run's build and setup logs: everything the platform did before the test
started.

Output: each line is `timestamp [stream] line`, where stream is `stdout` or
`stderr`. The whole build is streamed, so expect thousands of lines on a real
run. Grep the stream tag to narrow it, and read `[stderr]` first when a launch
failed.

Examples:
  snouty runs build-logs <run_id>
  snouty runs build-logs <run_id> | grep '\[stderr\]'
  snouty runs build-logs <run_id> | grep -i 'error\|denied'

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each log line prints as one JSON object
on its own line:
  snouty --json runs build-logs <run_id> | jq -r .text

Usage: snouty runs build-logs [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
